{
  "case_id": "2017-16-9493",
  "document_hash": "411f17f4c9aca5f84b32c0657d369493134839af276709f9aa40f6e5639aca9e",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-9493",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "411f17f4c9aca5f84b32c0657d369493134839af276709f9aa40f6e5639aca9e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-411f17f4c9ac-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:18 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Kristin L. Davidson",
      "case_id": "2017-16-9493",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "411f17f4c9aca5f84b32c0657d369493134839af276709f9aa40f6e5639aca9e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-411f17f4c9ac-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The government concedes that the Fifth Circuit's shocks-the-conscience standard is the wrong approach for a court of appeals to apply under the fourth prong of plain error review. The question remains: How should a court of appeals exercise its discretion when confronted with an obvious guidelines error that probably results in a defendant serving a longer prison sentence? We ask the Court to recognize what every circuit but the Fifth already has; that is, in the ordinary case, such an error seriously affects the fairness, integrity, and public reputation of the judicial proceedings and warrants correction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-9493",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "411f17f4c9aca5f84b32c0657d369493134839af276709f9aa40f6e5639aca9e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-411f17f4c9ac-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: We have said many times that correction under the plain error doctrine should be exercised sparingly, but I take it your argument is, in the context of a guidelines error, the discretion should not be exercised sparingly; it should be exercised routinely."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Kristin L. Davidson",
      "case_id": "2017-16-9493",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "411f17f4c9aca5f84b32c0657d369493134839af276709f9aa40f6e5639aca9e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-411f17f4c9ac-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. DAVIDSON: As the Court has recognized in Peugh and Molina-Martinez, the sentencing guidelines provide the essential framework for federal sentencing, and there is a well-documented anchoring effect so that when there is an erroneously high guidelines range, there's a significant risk that the defendant was sentenced to a longer prison time than he otherwise would have had the district court not been influenced by the error itself."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-9493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "411f17f4c9aca5f84b32c0657d369493134839af276709f9aa40f6e5639aca9e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-411f17f4c9ac-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That we've made ourselves?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Davidson",
      "case_id": "2017-16-9493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "411f17f4c9aca5f84b32c0657d369493134839af276709f9aa40f6e5639aca9e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-411f17f4c9ac-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes, especially when it results from an obvious and easily correctable error."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ellis",
      "case_id": "2017-16-9493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "411f17f4c9aca5f84b32c0657d369493134839af276709f9aa40f6e5639aca9e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-411f17f4c9ac-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Two courts of appeals have adopted presumptions, but even those courts have recognized that that presumption may be rebutted in case -- based on the factors that we've identified in our brief as grounds not to exercise the -- the court of appeals' authority."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-9493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "411f17f4c9aca5f84b32c0657d369493134839af276709f9aa40f6e5639aca9e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-411f17f4c9ac-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would it -- would it -- would it be ineffective assistance of counsel for counsel not to notice a glaring error in calculating the guidelines?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ellis",
      "case_id": "2017-16-9493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "411f17f4c9aca5f84b32c0657d369493134839af276709f9aa40f6e5639aca9e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-411f17f4c9ac-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One, there was an error. Two, it's clear and obvious. Three, it did affect the party's rights. He went to jail at least one day more."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ellis",
      "case_id": "2017-16-9493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "411f17f4c9aca5f84b32c0657d369493134839af276709f9aa40f6e5639aca9e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-411f17f4c9ac-0001-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Commission and the courts cooperate in gathering statistical information so that the Commission can see how that's working."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-9493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "411f17f4c9aca5f84b32c0657d369493134839af276709f9aa40f6e5639aca9e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-411f17f4c9ac-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think those are your choices, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-9493",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "411f17f4c9aca5f84b32c0657d369493134839af276709f9aa40f6e5639aca9e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-411f17f4c9ac-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: But I don't necessarily. Did we declare this -- this section unconstitutional in Booker? I mean, we tried to save as much as we could, and I don't know why we wouldn't have saved this one."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ellis",
      "case_id": "2017-16-9493",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "411f17f4c9aca5f84b32c0657d369493134839af276709f9aa40f6e5639aca9e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-411f17f4c9ac-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ELLIS: It was subsequently -\u00ad Justice Scalia subsequently wrote about it in a concurrence in Rita, and then the Court wrote about it in Footnote 7 of the majority opinion in Greenlaw."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-9493",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "411f17f4c9aca5f84b32c0657d369493134839af276709f9aa40f6e5639aca9e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-411f17f4c9ac-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: -- when -- when you're talking about reasonableness, it seems like you're doing substantive reasonableness, which is what the Fifth Circuit was doing with its standard."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Davidson",
      "case_id": "2017-16-9493",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "411f17f4c9aca5f84b32c0657d369493134839af276709f9aa40f6e5639aca9e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-411f17f4c9ac-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. DAVIDSON: I'd like to start with what Justice Breyer said about the guidelines as being a specialized body of guidance that has specialized proceedings."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-9493",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "411f17f4c9aca5f84b32c0657d369493134839af276709f9aa40f6e5639aca9e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-411f17f4c9ac-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:11 a.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
